<title>UK: London sugar freight sees a few new orders.</title>
<headline>London sugar freight sees a few new orders.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>No fixtures were reported on Friday in the London sugar freight market.</p>
<p>Among new orders E D and F Man had 6,000 tonnes bagged sugar Santander/Lattakia for mid-Jan and Dreyfus 14,000 bulk Thailand/S Korea end-Jan.</p>
<p>Other inquiry was from Czarnikow Rionda 12/14,000 bagged Thailand/Indonesia Jan/Feb and Jean Lion 14,000 bulk Cuba/Casablanca, Med or Black Sea Jan 15/30.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7729</p>
</text>
